codex
A shorter implementation gives a cleaner proof boundary: Python’s `set` establishes distinctness, `sorted` establishes order, and the conditional selects index 1 exactly when it exists. I’m switching to that equivalent implementation so the K semantics can define those built-ins explicitly and the universal claim can state the mathematical result directly, without a loop invariant axiom.
apply patch
